{"name":"Smoke on the Water","hex":"#9bacb3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"smoke","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The visible vapor/vapour, gases, and fine particles given off by burning or smoldering material.","A cigarette."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To inhale and exhale the smoke from a burning cigarette or cigar, burning material in a pipe, etc.","To inhale and exhale tobacco smoke."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smoke"},{"term":"water","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An inorganic compound (of molecular formula .mw-parser-output .template-chem2-su{display:inline-block;font-size:80%;line-height:1;vertical-align:-0.35em}.mw-parser-output .template-chem2-su>span{display:block;text-align:left}.mw-parser-output sub.template-chem2-sub{font-size:80%;vertical-align:-0.35em}.mw-parser-output sup.template-chem2-sup{font-size:80%;vertical-align:0.65em}H2O) found at room temperature and pressure as a clear liquid; it is present naturally as rain, and found in rivers, lakes and seas; its solid form is ice and its gaseous form is steam.","The liquid form of this substance: liquid H2O."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To wet or supply with water; to moisten; to overflow with water; to irrigate.\n\n  To pour water into the soil surrounding (plants).\n\n  To provide (animals) with water for drinking.","To pour water into the soil surrounding (plants)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/water"}],"entries":[{"title":"Smoke on the Water","blocks":[{"text":"\"Smoke on the Water\" is a song by English rock band Deep Purple, released on their 1972 studio album Machine Head. The song's lyrics are based on true events, chronicling the 1971 fire at Montreux Casino in Montreux, Switzerland. It is considered the band's signature song and its guitar riff is considered to be one of the most iconic in rock history."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ae/Smoke_on_the_Water_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smoke_on_the_Water","wikidata":"Q636399"},{"title":"Smoke on the Water (Red Foley song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Smoke on the Water\" is a song written by Zeke Clements and Earl Nunn and recorded by Red Foley in 1944. The patriotic song, which forecasts destruction for the Axis powers, particularly Japan, was Foley's first song to reach No. 1 on the Most-Played Juke Box Folk Records chart, spending 13 weeks at the top and a total of 24 weeks on the chart. \"Smoke on the Water\" also peaked at No. 7 on the Most-Played Juke Box Records chart. The B-side, \"There's a Blue Star Shining Bright \", peaked at No. 5 on the Most-Played Juke Box Folk Records chart."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smoke_on_the_Water_(Red_Foley_song)","wikidata":"Q7545910"},{"title":"Smoke","blocks":[{"text":"Smoke is an aerosol emitted when a material undergoes combustion or pyrolysis, together with the quantity of air that is entrained or otherwise mixed into the mass. It is commonly an unwanted by-product of fires, but may also be used for pest control (fumigation), communication, defensive and offensive capabilities in the military, cooking, or smoking. It is used in rituals where incense, sage, or resin is burned to produce a smell for spiritual or magical purposes. It can also be a flavoring agent and preservative."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Ognisko_ubt_0126.jpeg/330px-Ognisko_ubt_0126.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smoke","wikidata":"Q130768"},{"title":"Water","blocks":[{"text":"Water is an inorganic compound with the chemical formula H2O. It is a transparent, tasteless, odorless, and nearly colorless chemical substance. It is the main constituent of Earth's streams, lakes, and oceans. Water is also the fluid of all known living organisms, in which it acts as a solvent. Water, being a polar molecule, undergoes strong intermolecular hydrogen bonding which is a large contributor to its physical and chemical properties. It is vital for all known forms of life, despite not providing food energy or being an organic micronutrient. Due to its presence in all organisms, its chemical stability, its worldwide abundance, and its strong polarity relative to its small molecular size, water is often referred to as the \"universal solvent\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/H2O_2D_labelled.svg/330px-H2O_2D_labelled.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water","wikidata":"Q283"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Claude_Nobs1.jpg/500px-Claude_Nobs1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Claude_Nobs1.jpg/1280px-Claude_Nobs1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Claude_Nobs1.jpg/500px-Claude_Nobs1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Claude Nobs (2006), the \"Funky Claude\" mentioned in the song","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClaude_Nobs1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Smoke_on_the_water%2C_Montreux%2C_Switzerland_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Smoke_on_the_water%2C_Montreux%2C_Switzerland_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Smoke_on_the_water%2C_Montreux%2C_Switzerland_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-Smoke_on_the_water%2C_Montreux%2C_Switzerland_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Part of the now removed sculpture on the concrete wall next to the statue of Freddie Mercury","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASmoke_on_the_water%2C_Montreux%2C_Switzerland_-_panoramio.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c1/Smoke_on_the_Water_riff.jpg/500px-Smoke_on_the_Water_riff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c1/Smoke_on_the_Water_riff.jpg/500px-Smoke_on_the_Water_riff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The \"Smoke on the Water\" riff","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASmoke_on_the_Water_riff.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/5d/Smoke-on-the-water-armenia.jpg/250px-Smoke-on-the-water-armenia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5d/Smoke-on-the-water-armenia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/5d/Smoke-on-the-water-armenia.jpg/250px-Smoke-on-the-water-armenia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASmoke-on-the-water-armenia.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/78/Smoke-on-the-water-armenia-reissue.jpg/250px-Smoke-on-the-water-armenia-reissue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/78/Smoke-on-the-water-armenia-reissue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/78/Smoke-on-the-water-armenia-reissue.jpg/250px-Smoke-on-the-water-armenia-reissue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASmoke-on-the-wate